{
  "_comment": "Golden parity fixtures for routing chain intermediates into the run scratch: the plan rewrite that runs after the NL gates and before a skill's collision repair, for a skill whose skill.yaml sets `scratch_intermediates: true`. An intermediate is a step's `output` that a later step reads; it moves to `<work>/` keeping its place relative to the user's folder, and every later reference follows. An output nothing reads is a deliverable and stays; a file the user named in the request stays; with no utterance, every name is the caller's and nothing moves. Fixed plans in, the routed plan out, no model. `<work>` is the run's scratch folder and `<sandbox>` the folder paths resolve against; consumers substitute real directories and compare with `/` separators. Consumed by python/core/tests/test_scratch_routing_parity.py and native/crates/knaif-core/tests/scratch_routing_parity.rs. WHY: an intermediate left in the user's folder was one of the four leftover-file sources (36 ffmpeg rows, 129 files); both runtimes must move the same files to the same places, or the same utterance leaves different files behind.",
  "joining_tools": [
    "concat_video",
    "merge_pdfs"
  ],
  "_joining_tools": "Tools whose several inputs become ONE output (tools.yaml `joins_inputs: true`). A producer with a glob is never routed; one with several inputs is routed only when it joins them. Consumers pass this set.",
  "file_kinds": {
    "mp4": "video",
    "mov": "video",
    "gif": "video",
    "mp3": "audio",
    "aac": "audio",
    "jpg": "image",
    "pdf": "document",
    "txt": "text",
    "webm": "video",
    "avi": "video",
    "mkv": "video",
    "wav": "audio",
    "docx": "document",
    "html": "text"
  },
  "_file_kinds": "Extension -> kind, from each skill's skill.yaml `file_kinds:`. A reader writing another kind makes a new thing (see _derives).",
  "produces": {
    "extract_audio": "audio",
    "create_thumbnail": "image",
    "convert_document": {
      "arg": "to_format"
    },
    "convert_video": {
      "arg": "container"
    },
    "extract_text": "text"
  },
  "_produces": "What a tool writes (tools.yaml `produces:`): a kind, or {arg: <name>} when the kind follows an argument naming an extension. The declaration decides over the output's extension (the skill's word over the model's); a tool declaring nothing, or an {arg} without a usable value, follows its output's extension. For the request signal, the extension a reader writes is its output's, else the {arg} value; unknown counts as the same format.",
  "derives": [
    "trim_video",
    "concat_video",
    "split_pdf",
    "merge_pdfs"
  ],
  "_derives": "Tools whose output is a NEW thing made from the input (tools.yaml `derives: true`): a piece, a page range, a join. The keep rule (owner, 2026-10-15): an unnamed intermediate stays when the user asked for it. Tool signal: every reader makes a new thing (another kind, or a tool that derives). Request signal: the user named its format as a bare word (not inside a filename, not the producer's own input extension) and no reader writes that format again. Otherwise a reader refines it and it moves to the scratch.",
